 702:     #  #367: the path assertion, printed as its own row so the gate can name it.
 703:     #
 704:     #  The name gets a " path" SUFFIX, and that is load-bearing rather than
 705:     #  cosmetic. The gate greps named rows as "^<name>  .*ok$" -- TWO spaces --
 706:     #  so a path row printed under the bare name would give every one of the 22
 707:     #  existing named checks a count of 2 where it expects 1, turning the whole
 708:     #  section red. The suffix puts a single space after the base name, which
 709:     #  that pattern cannot match, so the value checks stay exact and the path
 710:     #  rows get their own names. The longest becomes 31 chars
 711:     #  ("A wb regofs post1 unal x10 path"), still inside the %-32s column, and
 712:     #  the format's two literal spaces keep the gate pattern satisfiable
 713:     #  regardless of padding.
 714:     lswant += 1
 715:     exp = LSGEN.get(name, 0)
 716:     seen = got.get("_lsgen")
 717:     lsok = (seen is not None and seen == exp)
 718:     lsgot += lsok
