codex
The debugger uses the ARM CPU’s byte order for `put w` and invalidates translated code on RAM writes. It also clears dyntrans state when entering interactive debugging. I found two ARM details that matter here: register names use aliases such as `sl` and `fp`, and the CPU constructor writes an additional PROM-emulation word near the top of RAM.
